From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:26:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: cluster-pwrgate: report the words of a
 disabled node

The J604 describes its CPU cluster power gates with the node disabled
until a probe of the two words on the machine shows what they hold: the
layout is T8140's, and nothing should be written on a guess. A deep
sleep needs the boot CPU's cluster enable set, so that probe is now in
the way of suspend-to-RAM.

For a node that is present but disabled, read each word and log it,
without writing anything. An enabled node is handled as before.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/apple/apple-cluster-pwrgate.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-cluster-pwrgate.c b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-cluster-pwrgate.c
index 67d493cff8..521bff7af8 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-cluster-pwrgate.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-cluster-pwrgate.c
@@ -31,8 +31,18 @@ static int __init apple_cluster_pwrgate_init(void)
 		void __iomem *gate;
 		int i;
 
-		if (!of_device_is_available(np))
+		/*
+		 * A node left disabled until its words are known on a board: report
+		 * them, read-only, so that a boot shows what the boot loader left.
+		 */
+		if (!of_device_is_available(np)) {
+			for (i = 0; (gate = of_iomap(np, i)); i++) {
+				pr_info("%pOF: disabled, cluster %d power gate word %#x (not written)\n",
+					np, i, readl(gate));
+				iounmap(gate);
+			}
 			continue;
+		}
 
 		/* One word per cluster. Shared with the sleep code, so not claimed. */
 		for (i = 0; (gate = of_iomap(np, i)); i++) {
